./results/telemetry/github-snapshot/open-issues.json:1690:  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: stage43-ld-simultaneous-measurements -->\n### Target declarations\n\n- `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Simultaneous.lean:new` -\n  a point-reference sandwich lemma: coordinate polynomial PVMs individually\n  consistent with the coordinate marginals of one joint point PVM yield a\n  tuple-polynomial POVM whose evaluated tuple is consistent with that joint\n  point PVM, with an explicit `C * k * sqrt(\u03b4 + m*d/q)` bound.\n- Same file - a two-sided sandwich lemma: coordinate PVMs on Alice and Bob that\n  are pairwise consistent across the state yield sandwiched tuple POVMs that\n  are globally consistent, with the same one-square-root error shape.\n- Same file - reuse `polynomialAgreement_avg_le_mdq` under #132's polynomial\n  equivalence to discharge the distinct-polynomial collision hypothesis.\n- Same file - `directCoordinateMainFormal`: invoke\n  `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.mainFormal` for every `r : Fin D.k` with the strategy and\n  pass proof from #130/#131 and `directLdAuxParameter` from #133.\n- Same file - `exists_directSimultaneousPolynomialMeasurements`, constructing\n  `GA : DirectPolyMeasTuple D S.\u03b9A` and\n  `GB : DirectPolyMeasTuple D S.\u03b9B` whose two point-consistency defects and\n  global-consistency defect are bounded by the explicit transport envelope\n  absorbed in #133.\n\n### Paper and blueprint references\n\n- Simultaneous low-degree conclusion:\n  `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413-458`\n  and `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:139-164`.\n- Sandwiched simultaneous measurement:\n  `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:465-501` and\n  `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/Sandwich.lean:58-107`.\n- Mature scalar conclusion:\n  `references/ldt-paper/test_definition.tex:180-202` and\n  `MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/MainFormal.lean:300-327`.\n- Reusable Schwartz--Zippel bound:\n  `MIPStarRE/LDT/Preliminaries/PolynomialAgreement.lean:90-163`.\n- The paper-gap note applying to this packet is\n  `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`; this is the product\n  argument that discharges its open simultaneity warning.\n\nIndependent applications of `mainFormal` do not make the resulting coordinate\nPVMs commute. Define the tuple effects by the existing palindromic\n`sandwichProduct`; prove measurement validity and transfer factors across the\nbipartite state one at a time. The global/global bound must be proved directly\nfrom the coordinate global consistencies, rather than by a second square-root\ntriangle through point measurements. This keeps the envelope within the\n`b = 1/80000` scale allowed by #133.\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- #130 and #131 supply coordinate strategies and `PassesLowIndividualDegreeTest`.\n- #132 supplies polynomial, measurement, and `ConsRel` conversions.\n- #133 supplies the auxiliary parameter and scalar envelope.\n- #49 must merge for the core distance calculus; #99 must merge for\n  `sandwichProduct_isMeasurement` and its insertion estimates.\n- The packet handles arbitrary positive `D.k`; it does not restrict the public\n  theorem to the route's special value `k = 1`.\n\n### Acceptance\n\n- `mainFormal` is applied separately to all coordinates with no extra\n  hypotheses, and finite choice produces the two coordinate families.\n- `GA` and `GB` are valid POVMs for arbitrary `D.k`; no commutativity of the\n  coordinate PVMs is assumed.\n- All three required defects have a proved explicit bound that #133 turns into\n  `deltaLd a b \u03b5 D.q D.m D.d D.k`.\n- Direct Lean checks, full build, paper-gap checks, exact-head CI, and\n  independent review pass with no `sorry`, axiom, bypass, bridge, or external\n  theorem import.\n\n### Scope notes\n\nOwn only the new simultaneity file and necessary imports. Generalize sandwich\nmachinery only in this file unless a minimal reusable theorem clearly belongs\nbeside #99 after its owner merges. Do not change `mainFormal`, `deltaLd`, either\npublic soundness signature, or the paper mirror. Main locators are from\n`c1c0af4`.\n\n---\nStage 4.3 proof packet under #47.\n\nPrerequisites are recorded as GitHub issue dependencies (blocked_by); the bullets above are commentary.\n",
